received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:1467f366ae232cf9b961dfc54bb041f5e9d721fb26dcb6f23fe9bb044c02a11a","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-19T22:21:37Z","updated_at":"2026-11-19T22:21:37Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m143-v0.14.3/m14stage3-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m143-v0.14.3","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m143-v0.14.3","body":"# Engacer OS M14.3 / 0.14.3 - Windows files and persistent settings\n\nDevelopment media passes **M14-STAGE3-VM-v1** native qualification. Complete GitHub and actual website delivery is recorded separately in the current status. Read the bounded scope below before testing.\n\nThis stage implements checked Unicode paths and enumeration, kernel-owned generation-checked shared file grants, existing-file edits, synchronous byte-range locks, durable user registry values, copied process environments and temporary files. User file metadata is independent of app ownership. Application instructions execute through Engacer OS's own kernel and compatibility APIs; there is no embedded Windows guest.\n\nBuild: `ee751b3d701e676254defe24d88acf67`, binding 642 compiled inputs.\n\n- ISO SHA-256: `d87ef78cca0bf6fb5674273fb577b0aed1de4c23cf5c067e92a0a1b4e2adde2d`\n- VMware ZIP SHA-256: `210a2498cd903d30337838fafe268f05813cda4ae52e683fd658bf919de78ec2`\n\nThe exact prepared ZIP passes owned headless VMware setup, restart with the ISO retained and two independent disk-only starts, with all shipped devices enabled and real guest input. Fresh compact 128-MiB, ordinary and actual 3840x2160 profiles also pass. Its disk is blank, growable 20-GiB SATA; the profile uses two CPUs and x64 UEFI with Secure Boot disabled. Installation erases the selected disposable disk. These named virtual tests do not establish universal hardware compatibility.\n\nThe original supported 7-Zip console/MSI installation, archive/extraction, removal and reinstallation pass, including all 106 original payload hashes. Original Notepad++ and SumatraPDF images remain inspection-only. Firefox remains a verified optional installer download; installation and execution are unavailable. Original Windows GUI and reusable MSI/EXE installer services follow in later M14 stages.\n\nThe selected file profile admits 128 shared objects and 32 grants per process, with lazy sparse dirty data capped globally at 8 MiB and logical file size capped at 64 MiB. Unicode simple-fold identity uses one 3,344-byte read-only kernel table. Search handles have sixteen generation-checked slots per process. The user registry bounds keys to 64, values to 128 and exact data to 2,048 bytes/value. Environment blocks grow lazily to 8,192 UTF-16 units with 64 variables. Unsupported device/network namespaces, full NTFS/reparse/ACL behavior, directory rename and asynchronous file I/O are not claimed.\n\nAll 29 matching native groups and five supporting host groups pass. Twenty-cycle resource checks retain zero managed pages after initialization. The file/lock/registry state-lifetime test repeats normal exit, UI cancellation and unhandled fault 21 times each, with four initial transition pages then zero retention, no remaining shared objects or temporary files, and acknowledged settings verified after independent starts. The blocked four-process profile observes 28 root/32 child metadata pages and peaks at 609 group-owned pages, with both guest CPUs halted. This is component accounting, not total OS RAM or original GUI performance. [Native acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/evidence/M14/3/acceptance-results.json), [resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/evidence/M14/3/resources.json). No faster-than-Windows claim is made. M14.15 remains the mandatory whole-system CPU/RAM/storage optimization gate.\n\n[Installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/docs/handbook/install-m143.md), [first day](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/docs/handbook/first-day-m143.md), [Windows files and browser downloads](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/docs/handbook/windows-m143.md), [implementation and exact development evidence](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/docs/architecture/files-m143.md), [stage gates](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/docs/milestones/m14-3.md), [ordered program](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a0ce3941901a2e92afc7f53f51622fa1a7fcfbdb/docs/milestones/m14.md).\n\nUse the matching [prepared VMware ZIP](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m143-v0.14.3/EngacerOS-M14STAGE3-VMware.zip), [ISO](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m143-v0.14.3/EngacerOS-M14STAGE3.iso) and [complete checksums](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m143-v0.14.3/M14STAGE3-SHA256SUMS.txt).\n"}